<description>
Copy the complete colored annotation from the fully marked motif onto each red-anchored copy.

Input structure
- The background surrounds several 8-connected foreground motifs.
- Every motif contains the same structural skeleton color and exactly one shared anchor-color pixel.
- Exactly one motif also contains the other marker colors; the remaining motifs contain only the skeleton and anchor.

Rule
- Use the fully marked motif as the source template.
- For each incomplete motif, find the unique rotation/reflection and translation that maps the source skeleton and anchor pixel onto the target skeleton and anchor pixel.
- Stamp all non-skeleton source marker pixels through that alignment, leaving the skeleton cells unchanged.

Key insight
- The anchor pixel fixes the orientation of an otherwise reusable skeleton, so the same local marker pattern can be transferred by a dihedral transform.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "fully annotated foreground motif s with a yellow skeleton, red anchor, and other marker pixels",
  "dst": "incomplete motifs d with the same yellow skeleton and only the red anchor",
  "match_cond": "s.skeleton and s.anchor align to d.skeleton and d.anchor under a unique rotation/flip/translation",
  "transform": "stamp all transformed non-skeleton marker pixels from s onto each d"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 13-15 rows x 13-15 cols, bg=0
  colors: bg=0, skeleton=4, anchor=2, markers={1,3} [observed — solver infers roles dynamically]
  motifs:
    count: 3-4 total (1 reference + 2-3 incomplete targets)
    skeleton: 4-connected polyomino, 5-6 cells, fits in 3-5 x 2-5 bbox
    anchor: exactly 1 pixel per motif, color shared across all, appears once per motif
    markers: 3-5 extra-color pixels on bg cells 8-adjacent to skeleton (reference only)
    marker_colors: 2 distinct colors [observed]
    structure: all motifs are distinct dihedral (rot90/flip) variants of the same skeleton+anchor shape
    uniqueness: skeleton+anchor combo must have >=N distinct dihedral variants where N = motif count
    asymmetry: anchor breaks skeleton symmetry so each target has exactly 1 valid alignment
  layout:
    motifs separated by >=4 Manhattan distance
    stamped markers land on bg cells within grid bounds, no overlap with other motifs
  transform:
    find unique dihedral alignment mapping reference skeleton+anchor onto each target
    stamp transformed marker pixels onto target (on bg cells), skeleton unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Design a 4-connected skeleton polyomino (5-6 cells) and place anchor on a bg cell 8-adjacent to it
    2. Verify skeleton+anchor has enough dihedral variants (>=N for N=3-4 motifs)
    3. Place 3-5 marker pixels (2 colors) on bg cells 8-adjacent to skeleton to form the reference patch
    4. Pick N-1 distinct dihedral variants for target motifs; for each, compute transformed marker positions
    5. Choose grid size 13-15 x 13-15; place all motifs (reference + targets) with >=4 Manhattan separation
    6. Verify all transformed marker positions land on bg cells within grid bounds (this is the output)
    7. Remove marker pixels from target motifs to produce the input (targets keep only skeleton+anchor)
```
